# mapping_set_description: skos:exactMatch is emitted only where mapping_justification is semapv:LexicalMatching; mappings justified by embedding similarity are capped at skos:closeMatch.
# other: The LLM backend is not deterministic at temperature=0, so this set is ONE SAMPLE rather than a function of its inputs. Two identical runs were measured to disagree on 2.7% of the rows both kept (54/1993, 2026-08-16); treat a smaller difference between two sets as noise. src/relation_audit.py --compare DIR_A DIR_B lists the rows that moved, which are the ones a reviewer should look at first.
# refine_filter: refine Rule 5 removed broad/narrow mappings entailed by a source-concept ancestor's exact/close match; flags: defaults
